  {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "All 81 tests pass and the project builds cleanly.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe issue was in the \u0060terminal_panel\u0060 function in \u0060src/main.rs\u0060. There was a \u0060use_future\u0060 loop that listened for \u0060title_changed\u0060 events from the embedded terminal:\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060rust\n_ = terminal_handle.title_changed().fuse() =\u003E {\n    if let Some(new_title) = terminal_handle.title() {\n        Platform::get().with_window(None, move |window| {\n            window.set_title(\u0026new_title);\n        });\n    }\n}\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\nThe terminal\u0027s shell reports its title via the \u0060title_changed\u0060 event, and shells typically set their title to something like \u0060username@hostname:~/path\u0060. This handler was **overriding the window title** with the shell\u0027s title every time it changed, which is why the title always showed the username instead of staying as \u0022RustAgent\u0022 (or whatever you set it to).\n\n**The fix:** I removed the \u0060title_changed\u0060 handler from the \u0060use_future\u0060 loop. Now the window title stays as the \u0060\u0022RustAgent\u0022\u0060 title set in \u0060main()\u0060 via \u0060WindowConfig::new(app).with_title(\u0022RustAgent\u0022)\u0060, and it\u0027s no longer overwritten by the terminal\u0027s shell title.\n\nThe \u0060closed\u0060, \u0060clipboard_changed\u0060, and \u0060output_received\u0060 handlers were left intact, so terminal closing, clipboard sync, and the file-tree\u0027s cwd tracking (via OSC 7) all still work correctly.\n\nTask complete.",
